=== Report ===
The information presented centers around nucleotide sequences and relevant parameters associated with primer design in molecular biology applications such as PCR amplification. Each entry consists of a sequence identifier, the corresponding 5'-3' nucleotide sequence, product size (in base pairs), annealing temperature, and melting temperature (Tm).

Close examination of the sequences reveals two pairs, each with one named and one unnamed sequence. "SmW2REPM (W2)" is paired with an unnamed sequence, and "SCMDNAP (W1)" is similarly paired. In both cases, the named entries contain complete information including expected product size (395 bp for W2, 316 bp for W1), annealing temperatures (both at 59°C), and Tm values (63.9°C for W2 and 64.8°C for W1). The unnamed sequences present only the nucleotide sequences and melting temperatures (64.1°C and 63.8°C), with the remaining fields unpopulated.

This pattern suggests a conventional forward and reverse primer arrangement. Typically, the identifier marks one primer, while its counterpart—often unnamed—serves as the complementary primer for the amplification reaction. The melting temperatures of both pairs are closely aligned, indicating optimized primer compatibility and likely efficiency in amplification under the chosen conditions.

For clarity, the table below summarizes these vital attributes as they appear in the original information: ## Sheet: Sheet1

| [Person_1]    | 5'-3' sequences      |   Product Size |   Annealing temp |   Tm |
|:--------------|:---------------------|---------------:|-----------------:|-----:|
| SmW2REPM (W2) | GTGCAGTTTGCCGATGTCTA |            395 |               59 | 63.9 |
| nan           | CACAGCTCCTTCGATCATCA |            nan |              nan | 64.1 |
