Similarly, BNP Paribas (BNPP) demonstrates a comparable tier structure, with CET1 values climbing from 20 to 120 across the same tier labels. Notably, this indicates a more conservative starting point compared to GS’s unsatisfactory threshold at 5, suggesting differing baseline capital positions or risk-appetite benchmarks between the two banks.

