=== Report ===
The financial snapshot presented highlights a significant interplay between sales, costs, and resulting profit or loss categories. The gross sales figure stands at $100,000, while the total costs are accounted for at $50,000. This margin directly informs the categorization of financial outcomes into losses or profits based on specified thresholds.

Financial performance is segmented into distinct rating brackets that correspond to ranges of net profit or loss, defined in terms of dollar amounts. For instance, a net loss exceeding $10,000 is labeled as a "Large loss," whereas smaller deficits falling between $0 and -$10,000 are characterized as a "Small loss." Conversely, outcomes that break even at zero net gain or loss receive the "Break even" classification. On the profitable side, gains between greater than zero but less than $10,000 are considered a "Small profit," while profits exceeding $100,000 qualify as a "Large profit."

This tiered rule system offers a straightforward mechanism for evaluating financial health, simplifying decision-making around business performance by coupling quantitative outcomes with qualitative labels. The conditional logic embedded in the evaluation ensures that any net financial figure is mapped to the appropriate category.

