=== Report ===
A review of the current assortment of items available for sale reveals several notable patterns in pricing, cost structure, and product differentiation. The core product groups—NSB, SPB, PP, and OSB—each have multiple color variations with pricing that reflects either uniformity across a group or incremental differentiation.

For the NSB line (Black, Orange, Blue), the retail price is set at $16.99 for each color variant, each carrying a consistent cost of $3.50. This suggests a strategic positioning aimed at maintaining margin consistency regardless of color option, possibly to simplify both pricing communication to customers and back-end inventory management.

Similarly, most SPB items maintain this $16.99 price point and $3.50 cost, with the exception of the Orange and Green variants, which are priced slightly higher at $17.99. The uniform cost across all SPB products indicates that the price differential is marketing- or demand-driven rather than a reflection of cost variance.

The PP product stands out for its lower price of $11.99 and correspondingly lower cost of $3.00, distinguishing it from the rest as an entry-level or more competitively positioned option.

Meanwhile, the OSB range follows a tight price clustering: all color variants are offered at $12.99 with a cost of $5.00 each. This higher cost-to-price ratio may reflect greater material or production costs, or perhaps premium features associated with this line.

A detailed breakdown of current offerings, prices, and costs is provided in the following table: ## Sheet: Sheet1

