The presented figures illuminate the movement and distribution of holdings across four key regions: London, Beijing, Tokyo, and the US. Notably, the data differentiates internal transfers—movements of holdings between these regions—from external transfers, which involve adjustments without corresponding inbound or outbound counterparts within the set.

At the core of the internal transfer activity is a sizable transaction of 2,030 units from London to Tokyo, reflected precisely in both cities' holdings and transfer totals. Beijing, meanwhile, shows a heavier accumulation of holdings with 131,218 units attributed internally, though without corresponding transfer activity outbound, suggesting a stable internal position or inflow from other regions outside the internal transfer scope.

