From the pricing data, it is clear that as IOPS requirements increase, customers benefit from a graduated discount structure on IOPS costs, incentivizing higher provisioning for workloads demanding substantial throughput. The flat storage rate maintains a steady base cost, emphasizing how IOPS-related charges can significantly influence monthly billing.

An illustrative hypothetical calculation underscores this pattern:

| IOPS Range               | Rate (USD per IOPS/month) | IOPS Count | Subtotal IOPS Cost (USD) |
