Could you extract the classroom demand analysis data—including section size ranges, required and available rooms, capacity figures, and calculated balances—from the institutional scheduling report, and present it in JSON following the provided schema and structure?

=== Report ===
This report assesses instructional space needs and scheduling considerations for academic programming, structured to support efficient allocation of classroom resources. The following analysis synthesizes the information presented in the formal demand summary, including both operational conventions and capacity breakdowns.

The analysis is premised on established scheduling norms detailed within the report: a standard semester consists of 16 weeks, each class period encompasses 50 minutes, and instructional activities are distributed across 35 periods per week. These parameters form the benchmark against which classroom utilization and requirements are evaluated.

Class sections are organized by enrollment ranges, escalating from a minimum cohort of 1–13 students to the largest category exceeding 175 students per section. Each range is associated with a corresponding maximum room capacity, spanning from rooms designed for 20 students up to those accommodating 225. This stratification enables tailored assignment of instructional spaces to course demand, optimizing usage and minimizing resource mismatch.

The structure of the demand analysis—illustrated in ## Sheet: Sheet1

| CLASSROOM DEMAND ANALYSIS REPORT                                                                                            | Unnamed: 1   | Unnamed: 2                            | Unnamed: 3   | Unnamed: 4   | Unnamed: 5   | SCHEDULING STANDARDS   | Unnamed: 7                | Unnamed: 8   |
|:----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:-------------|:--------------------------------------|:-------------|:-------------|:-------------|:-----------------------|:--------------------------|:-------------|
| UW -                                                                                                                        | nan          | [INSERT YOUR INSTITUTION'S NAME HERE] | nan          | nan          | nan          | 16                     | :WEEKS/SEMESTER           | nan          |
| ACADEMIC TERM:                                                                                                              | nan          | [INSERT FALL/SPRING 200# HERE]        | nan          | nan          | nan          | 50                     | :MINUTES/PERIOD           | nan          |
| DATE:                                                                                                                       | nan          | [INSERT TODAY'S DATE HERE]            | nan          | nan          | nan          | 35                     | :PERIODS/WEEK INSTRUCTION | nan          |
| nan                                                                                                                         | nan          | TOTAL                                 | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| nan                                                                                                                         | nan          | REQUIRED                              | MAXIMUM      | TOTAL        | NO. OF       | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| SECTION                                                                                                                     | TOTAL        | ROOM                                  | ROOM         | REQUIRED     | AVAILABLE    | nan                    | PLANNED                   | ADJUSTED     |
| SIZE                                                                                                                        | SECTIONS     | PERIODS                               | CAPACITY     | ROOMS        | ROOMS        | BALANCE                | ADJUST                    | BALANCE      |
| 001 - 013                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 20           | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 014 - 027                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 40           | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 028 - 040                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 55           | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 041 - 053                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 70           | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 054 - 068                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 90           | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 069 - 088                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 110          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 089 - 131                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 150          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 132 - 174                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 200          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| 175 - 196                                                                                                                   | nan          | nan                                   | 225          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| TOTALS                                                                                                                      | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| NOTES:                                                                                                                      | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| SECTION SIZE = range for number of students enrolled in a scheduled class section                                           | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| TOTAL SECTIONS = total number of scheduled class sections in a particular size range                                        | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| TOTAL REQUIRED ROOM PERIODS = total number of room periods scheduled for a particular size range (1 credit = 1 room period) | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| ROOM CAPACITY = fixed field, maximum room capacity…calculated based on SECTION SIZE and planned occupancy %                 | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| TOTAL REQUIRED ROOMS = TOTAL ROOM PERIODS / CLASSROOM USE STANDARD                                                          | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| NO. OF AVAILABLE ROOMS = number of rooms available for scheduled class sections in a particular size range                  | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| BALANCE = NO. OF AVAILABLE ROOMS - TOTAL REQUIRED ROOMS                                                                     | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| ADJUSTMENT = proposed adjustments to classroom sizes to accomodate class scheduling needs                                   | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
| ADJUSTED BALANCE = BALANCE + PLANNED ADJUSTMENT                                                                             | nan          | nan                                   | nan          | nan          | nan          | nan                    | nan                       | nan          |
—enumerates room requirements, total section counts, and available instructional spaces for each section size grouping. For each category, the assessment considers the classroom capacity required, juxtaposes this against the count of rooms available, and calculates any resulting surplus or shortage. The mechanism for balance computation (i.e., available rooms minus rooms required) is explicitly described, facilitating rapid identification of potential bottlenecks or excesses within the existing physical inventory.

Supplementary notes clarify key calculation methodologies, emphasizing that “room periods” are proportionally aligned to credit assignments (one credit equates to one room period), and classroom use standards are essential in translating section room-period needs into concrete room counts. The system allows for flexibility through “planned adjustment” numbers, enabling dynamic adaptation should a scheduled need outstrip supply or, conversely, free up resources as program structures evolve.

For illustration, consider a hypothetical scenario: if the “041–053” section size range requires 10 rooms for a given semester, but only 8 are available, the balance would be –2, highlighting a shortfall. Should a planned adjustment add 2 rooms to the inventory (through rescheduling or conversion), the adjusted balance returns to equilibrium at zero. The following fabricated table illustrates such an example, though the figures are illustrative and do not represent actual counts:

