=== Report ===
This report examines a series of samples linked to distinct entities, characterized by identifiers and timeframes related to hospital admissions and discharges. The objective is to associate each sample with the correct related numerical code (id2), determined by verifying that the sample’s timestamp falls within the corresponding admission-to-discharge interval of its primary entity.

A total of three principal identifiers, labeled A, B, and C, are tracked over varying periods from 2001 to 2010. Each sample is timestamped, and multiple sub-identifiers (id1.1) correspond to individual cases or samples under each main entity. The challenge lies in correctly mapping the sample to the id2 code based on whether the sample date occurs during that entity’s hospitalization interval.

For example, entity A includes samples taken in early 2001, 2004, and 2007, interlaced with hospital stays spanning adjacent years. Entity B shows a series of samples mostly from 2002 to 2005, with admission and discharge dates occurring across several consecutive years. Entity C’s records extend through 2006 to 2010, again with synchronized admissions and sample dates.

The logic for assigning the id2 code rests on ensuring the sample date is inclusive of the admission date and discharge date for that period, thus linking the sample to the corresponding hospital visit. This naturally helps in identifying the valid id2 value among potentially multiple time intervals for the same id1.

To illustrate, some samples related to entity A, such as a sample taken on January 2, 2001, corresponds correctly to an admission occurring on January 1, 2001, ending in February 2001. Another sample with id1.1 code C, sampled in January 2004, aligns with an admission spanning 2003–2004. Conversely, samples that do not fall within any admission period lack a valid id2 association.

The table below synthesizes these observations by showing each sample’s primary identifier, sample date, sub-identifier, associated id2, and the admission and discharge dates that justify the link:

