| The date of sample needs to be between the date of admission and date of discharge for each id1, to give the correct id2 number. | NaT                 | nan     |     nan | NaT                 | NaT                 |
| Thanks!                                                                                                                          | NaT                 | nan     |     nan | NaT                 | NaT                 |


This data structure allows mapping temporal relationships seamlessly, indicating when patients or entities were under care relative to sample collection moments. It enables precise retrieval of the related numerical code, critical for downstream analysis or operational workflows that depend on accurate event-to-admission linkages.

To appreciate this further, consider an illustrative simplified scenario where another dataset contains admission-discharge intervals for three entities, and a set of sample dates is used to validate correct association with these intervals. Such an approach is commonplace in longitudinal clinical or operational studies where time-bound events must be matched with episodes of care or service usage.

