=== Report ===
This report addresses the framework and compliance criteria for middle school student classification within an athletics program for San Antonio Independent School District (SAISD) middle schools. The classification system is designed to maintain consistent eligibility standards across schools, grades, and sports participation, ensuring fair competition and adherence to age-based regulations.

The eligibility criteria specify that participation is restricted to students in 7th and 8th grades who have not reached certain age thresholds by September 1 of the current school year. Specifically, 7th graders must be younger than 14 years old as of that date; any 7th grader aged 14 or older competes as an 8th grader. Similarly, 8th graders must be younger than 15 years old to participate, and those who have reached 15 by September 1 are ineligible for competition in this program. Sixth graders are categorically excluded from participation, irrespective of age.

This age classification system serves to preserve competitive balance and safeguard the integrity of the middle school athletics program. Exceptions to these age and grade restrictions are subject to administrative approval by designated officials, including the Director of Athletics, thereby providing a controlled mechanism for handling extraordinary cases.

The organizational structure includes fields for student name, birthdate, student ID number, and age, facilitating accurate tracking and monitoring of eligibility requirements. Additional administrative roles such as principal, coordinator, and coach are also designated with signature approval lines to formalize compliance and accountability.

