When viewed against such benchmarks, the actual values fall short in several domains, particularly relating to feedback and marking transparency—implicating these as sustained development priorities.

In summary, the data indicates that students within this faculty experienced a noticeable downturn in satisfaction and engagement in the middle year, with partial recovery thereafter. Persistent challenges around feedback and learning support, evidenced by consistently lower ratings, suggest these aspects warrant ongoing attention. The broad pattern implies that while certain acute issues were addressed after 2009/0, the restoration of initial confidence in all areas remains incomplete.

